<h1>Sara Feigenholtz</h1>
<p>Illinois Senate, 6th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic. Incumbent.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.sarafeigenholtz.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (sarafeigenholtz.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Her campaign site lists education access, public safety including an assault weapons ban, health care and senior care, abortion access and LGBTQ rights, and renewable energy and climate as her priorities. She won the March 2026 Democratic primary over Nick Uniejewski with about 56 percent of the vote.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>A full-time legislator, she served in the Illinois House from 1995 to 2020 before being appointed to the Senate seat in 2020.</p>
